  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The main point of having likes and dislikes on worlds is to show other people what you thought of a world, good and bad. There are going to be times where worlds are review bombed much like videos on YouTube have been, but when YouTube removed the dislike counter, *nobody* was on board with that. Honestly the dislikes should be visible unless it becomes a widespread problem for most creators. Dislikes as a self-referential guide has always been secondary. Please make both scores visible to all users.\n\nHere's a free idea to help counter any review-botting/bombing: Don't let the ranks of Visitor, New User, or Nuisance vote on worlds. That's it. Obviously it's not going to prevent all of it, but it will prevent bot accounts from mass-downvoting worlds.",
